<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Biome opt-in, generic from day one (RULED, MOVING_DUNES_DESIGN.md §5): the engine
    mod itself binds vanilla Desert and ExtremeDesert to its own generic sand material.
    Campaign biomes are bound by the RUT data pack, not here.

    PatchOperationAddModExtension is the vanilla operation for exactly this; it appends
    to <modExtensions> and creates the node if the def has none, so it works on a def
    that has never carried an extension.

    Neither operation is guarded: both target vanilla core BiomeDefs that are always
    present, so a false return is a real failure worth the log line. A Conditional or
    FindMod wrapper here would only convert a broken binding into silence — both of
    those return true on no match, which is the trap this repo's rules name first.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="Desert"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.MovingDunes.DuneFieldExtension">
        <material>RM_Dunes_Sand</material>
      </li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ExtremeDesert"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.MovingDunes.DuneFieldExtension">
        <material>RM_Dunes_Sand</material>
      </li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!--
    STILLSAND_RULED_CONTENT_1 (2026-09-27 sitting, §7/Rulings Q12 RATIFIED, owner's
    own wording: "bind RM_Stillsand (and the frozen twin until Phase B) into
    mandrake.rm.movingdunes"). Neither vanilla Desert nor vanilla ExtremeDesert is
    actually used on Ash'karr, so the two bindings above are inert on the live world —
    this engine has been wired to NO Ash'karr biome until now (measured this pass,
    matching the item's own finding). RUT_ExtremeDesert itself is NOT touched anywhere
    else — it stays frozen (R22) until Phase B's repaint retires it; this is purely an
    additive binding on top.

    Unlike the two vanilla operations above, RM_Stillsand and RUT_ExtremeDesert are
    NOT guaranteed present in every mod list this engine mod could load into on its
    own (this file's own header: "the engine mod itself binds vanilla... campaign
    biomes are bound by the RUT data pack, not here" — Q12 deliberately overrides
    that default for these two specific biomes, at the owner's explicit direction, but
    the safety concern the default was protecting against still applies). So these two
    are wrapped in PatchOperationConditional, the correct gating idiom this repo uses
    elsewhere (never a top-level MayRequire, which is inert on an Operation node) —
    on a mod list with neither Stillsand nor Ashkarr/Utinni content loaded, the xpath
    simply matches nothing and both Operations no-op cleanly instead of logging a
    hard xpath-not-found error.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Stillsand"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Stillsand"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.MovingDunes.DuneFieldExtension">
          <material>RM_Dunes_Sand</material>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RUT_ExtremeDesert"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RUT_ExtremeDesert"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.MovingDunes.DuneFieldExtension">
          <material>RM_Dunes_Sand</material>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
